      "id": "0ee7893d-4d38-460b-90a0-7a78b971bc95",
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "No \u2014 `template/configs.py` is identical to `solar_event/configs.py` (both define `FlareDataConfig`), and per the repo's downstream pattern, you're supposed to **copy the template to build a new app, not edit the template in place**. Since `solar_event/` already exists as its own app with its own `configs.py`, `datasets/solar_event_dataset.py`, etc., you should:\n\n- Edit `downstream_apps/solar_event/configs.py` (rename `flare_index_path` \u2192 whatever your YAML uses, e.g. `solar_event_path`, or vice versa \u2014 rename the YAML key to match `flare_index_path`).\n- Leave `downstream_apps/template/` untouched \u2014 it's the generic starting point other future apps will copy, not something `solar_event` should be modifying.\n\nSo: fix the mismatch in `solar_event/configs.py` (or its YAML), not in `template/configs.py`.",
      "mentions": [],
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona"
