            "raw_output": "/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/0_dataset_dataloader_template.ipynb:71:     \"evalue\": \"cannot import name 'solar_event_path' from 'downstream_apps.solar_event.configs' (/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/../../downstream_apps/solar_event/configs.py)\",\n/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/0_dataset_dataloader_template.ipynb:76:      \"Cell \\u001b[0;32mIn[6], line 8\\u001b[0m\\n\\u001b[1;32m      1\\u001b[0m \\u001b[38;5;66;03m# The config is the single source of truth. load_flare_config() parses it into a typed\\u001b[39;00m\\n\\u001b[1;32m      2\\u001b[0m \\u001b[38;5;66;03m# object, exactly as the training script 3_finetune_template_1D.py does, so the same YAML\\u001b[39;00m\\n\\u001b[1;32m      3\\u001b[0m \\u001b[38;5;66;03m# behaves identically in the notebook and in production.\\u001b[39;00m\\n\\u001b[0;32m   (...)\\u001b[0m\\n\\u001b[1;32m      6\\u001b[0m \\u001b[38;5;66;03m# completion, and a misspelled key fails here with a list of the valid ones instead of\\u001b[39;00m\\n\\u001b[1;32m      7\\u001b[0m \\u001b[38;5;66;03m# silently doing nothing.\\u001b[39;00m\\n\\u001b[0;32m----> 8\\u001b[0m \\u001b[38;5;28;01mfrom\\u001b[39;00m\\u001b[38;5;250m \\u001b[39m\\u001b[38;5;21;01mdownstream_apps\\u001b[39;00m\\u001b[38;5;21;01m.\\u001b[39;00m\\u001b[38;5;21;01msolar_event\\u001b[39;00m\\u001b[38;5;21;01m.\\u001b[39;00m\\u001b[38;5;21;01mconfigs\\u001b[39;00m\\u001b[38;5;250m \\u001b[39m\\u001b[38;5;28;01mimport\\u001b[39;00m solar_event_path\\n\\u001b[1;32m     10\\u001b[0m cfg \\u001b[38;5;241m=\\u001b[39m solar_event_path(\\u001b[38;5;124m\\\"\\u001b[39m\\u001b[38;5;124m./configs/config_script.yaml\\u001b[39m\\u001b[38;5;124m\\\"\\u001b[39m)\\n\\u001b[1;32m     11\\u001b[0m \\u001b[38;5;28mprint\\u001b[39m(\\u001b[38;5;124mf\\u001b[39m\\u001b[38;5;124m\\\"\\u001b[39m\\u001b[38;5;124mLoaded config for job: \\u001b[39m\\u001b[38;5;132;01m{\\u001b[39;00mcfg\\u001b[38;5;241m.\\u001b[39mjob_id\\u001b[38;5;132;01m}\\u001b[39;00m\\u001b[38;5;124m\\\"\\u001b[39m)\\n\",\n/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/0_dataset_dataloader_template.ipynb:77:      \"\\u001b[0;31mImportError\\u001b[0m: cannot import name 'solar_event_path' from 'downstream_apps.solar_event.configs' (/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/../../downstream_apps/solar_event/configs.py)\"\n/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/0_dataset_dataloader_template.ipynb:89:    \"from downstream_apps.solar_event.configs import solar_event_path\\n\",\n/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/0_dataset_dataloader_template.ipynb:91:    \"cfg = solar_event_path(\\\"./configs/config_script.yaml\\\")\\n\",\n/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/configs.py:39:    solar_event_path: str = \"\"\n/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/configs/config_script.yaml:46:  solar_event_path: ../data/solar_event_data.csv\n/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/understanding dataloaders.chat:117:      \"body\": \"  solar_event_path: ../data/solar_event_data.csv\\n  ds_time_column: 'Start Date'      # Column in the flare catalog used as the event timestamp\\n  ds_time_tolerance: 4d           # Max allowed gap between catalog and Surya timestamps\\n  ds_match_direction: forward     # \\\"forward\\\": use solar state *before* the flare (causal)\\n\\nExplain each of these parameters in brief.\",\n/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/understanding dataloaders.chat:152:      \"body\": \"Quick flag: your snippet uses `solar_event_path`, but `FlareDataConfig` (in `configs.py`) defines the field as `flare_index_path`. Since unknown YAML keys raise an error (per CLAUDE.md), `solar_event_path` would fail to load \\u2014 you likely want to rename that key.\\n\\nHere's what each parameter does:\\n\\n- **`flare_index_path`** (you have `solar_event_path`) \\u2014 path to the flare catalog CSV (`ds_flare_index_path` in the dataset's `__init__`). Resolved relative to the config file's directory since it's listed in `PATH_FIELDS`.\\n\\n- **`ds_time_column: 'Start Date'`** \\u2014 which column in that CSV holds the event timestamp. Parsed to `datetime64` and used as the right-hand key in the `merge_asof` against Surya's `valid_indices`.\\n\\n- **`ds_time_tolerance: 4d`** \\u2014 max allowed time gap between a flare's timestamp and the nearest Surya frame. Matches beyond 4 days are dropped; if *no* matches survive, `__init__` raises `ValueError`.\\n\\n- **`ds_match_direction: forward`** \\u2014 direction passed to `pd.merge_asof`. `\\\"forward\\\"` pairs each flare with the *next* Surya timestamp at or after it... actually, checking `pd.merge_asof` semantics: `direction=\\\"forward\\\"` matches each left row (Surya `valid_indices`) to the *nearest ds_index at or after* it. Combined with the comment \\\"solar state before the flare,\\\" the intent is: for a given flare, find the Surya frame taken just before it, so the model predicts the flare from prior solar state \\u2014 this is what makes the task causal (no leakage of post-flare data into the input).\",\n/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/understanding dataloaders.chat:223:      \"body\": \"No \\u2014 `template/configs.py` is identical to `solar_event/configs.py` (both define `FlareDataConfig`), and per the repo's downstream pattern, you're supposed to **copy the template to build a new app, not edit the template in place**. Since `solar_event/` already exists as its own app with its own `configs.py`, `datasets/solar_event_dataset.py`, etc., you should:\\n\\n- Edit `downstream_apps/solar_event/configs.py` (rename `flare_index_path` \\u2192 whatever your YAML uses, e.g. `solar_event_path`, or vice versa \\u2014 rename the YAML key to match `flare_index_path`).\\n- Leave `downstream_apps/template/` untouched \\u2014 it's the generic starting point other future apps will copy, not something `solar_event` should be modifying.\\n\\nSo: fix the mismatch in `solar_event/configs.py` (or its YAML), not in `template/configs.py`.\",\n/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/understanding dataloaders.chat:228:      \"body\": \"ImportError: cannot import name 'solar_event_path' from 'downstream_apps.solar_event.configs' (/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/../../downstream_apps/solar_event/configs.py)\\n\\nWhy does this error occur even after correcting the configs.py to match the config_script.yaml file?\",",
